<title>UK: Cazenove Indian GDR Index dips.</title>
<headline>Cazenove Indian GDR Index dips.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Cazenove Indian GDR Index was down 0.46 points, or 0.69 percent, at 77.47 after the Bombay Stock Exchange 30 share index rose 41.46 points to 3,604.20.</p>
<p>The premium for GDRs over stocks on the local market was 9.45 percent from 11.93 percent on Monday.</p>
<p>The Cazenove index is a capitalisation weighted basket of Indian global depositary receipts and measures the change from midday on the previous trading day to midday today.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 5887</p>
